You'll see that we have a element with a top level heading inside it and a element containing three s. We're going to use these to create a fairly standard three column layout.

## Specifying what elements to lay out as flexible boxes

To start with, we need to select which elements are to be laid out as flexible boxes. To do this, we set a special value of on the parent element of the elements you want to affect. In this case we want to lay out the elements, so we set this on the :

```html hidden live-sample___flexbox_1

